//==
// # Decided geometric results
//
// TYPE-CATALOG.md section 5 (catalog merge, 2026-10-20): what a normal, a projection, a
// closest-point search, and a closure test return when they can and cannot answer.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Normals
//  - Projections and closest points
//  - Closure

//==
// # Normals

// What NormalAt and LimitNormal return in place of NormalOr(fallback).
//   Regular: the normal at an ordinary point.
//   Limit: the limit along the parameter line at a pole.
//   Apex: the limit normal at a cone's apex.
//   NoNormal: no normal and no limit, with the reason.
// Removes: the +z fallback that sent refinement toward the apex (F-57 item 2).
type SurfaceNormal
    = Regular(Normal: Direction3D)
    | Limit(Normal: Direction3D)
    | Apex(Normal: Direction3D)
    | NoNormal(Reason: UndecidedReason);

//==
// # Projections and closest points

// What Project returns.
//   OnSurface: the foot of the perpendicular lies in the domain.
//   OffDomain: the nearest point in the domain, which is not a perpendicular foot.
//   Failed: no point, with the reason.
// Removes: a projection outside the domain used as if inside.
type Projection
    = OnSurface(Uv: UvPoint, Distance: ModelLength)
    | OffDomain(Nearest: UvPoint, Distance: ModelLength)
    | Failed(Reason: UndecidedReason);

// What a closest-parameter search on a curve returns.
//   Found: one closest parameter.
//   Ambiguous: several parameters equally close (the centre of a circle).
//   Failed: no parameter, with the reason.
// Removes: the closest point on a circle taken at the antipode with no sign
// of trouble.
type ClosestParameterResult
    = Found(T: CurveParameter, Distance: ModelLength)
    | Ambiguous(Candidates: Array<CurveParameter>)
    | Failed(Reason: UndecidedReason);

//==
// # Closure

// What chunk D1's end-point rule decides about a curve's closure.
//   ClosedByEnds: the ends meet within tolerance; Gap is their distance.
//   OpenByEnds: the ends are farther apart than the tolerance.
//   ClosedByPeriod: the curve's family is periodic (a circle, an ellipse).
//   UndecidableWithoutEvaluation: the ends are not known without evaluating.
// Removes: closure decided by sampling a curve.
type ClosureDecision
    = ClosedByEnds(Gap: ModelLength)
    | OpenByEnds(Gap: ModelLength)
    | ClosedByPeriod
    | UndecidableWithoutEvaluation;
